{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/857396-recs-for-polaris","id":857396,"title":"Recs for Polaris?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-01T19:03:27-07:00","id":857396,"title":"Recs for Polaris?","content":"Is anyone familiar with French RPGs? I'm eyeing the kickstarter for <b>Polaris</b>, an undersea/sci-fi game. But I'm having trouble finding details on it, beyond the Kickstarter press release. Apparently there's a fantasy game with the same name (set at the North Pole), and that's all I'm finding . . . Anyway, anyone familiar with the underwater game? Or have a good source for French RPG reviews?<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: This is the one I'm looking for details on:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><i>The Polaris RPG</i></b> is set in a far future where the world above ground has become uninhabitable for the human species. Human beings have found refuge in the depths of the ocean, where they try to somehow survive in spite of the many difficulties they encounter in this hostile environment. The species\u2019 degeneration (characterized by the increasing number of sterile individuals and various genetic mutations), the perpetual wars that have ravaged entire colonies, the monsters, and, above all, the difficulty of exploiting natural resources are the immediate problems faced by this civilization.<br /> <br /> In this new world of silence and darkness, players can choose to become agents of one of the underwater factions, mercenaries working to keep afloat, or freelancers trying to establish their own communities. . . </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 04-01-2016, 1